  "rule": "Calls without a slice root, or descriptor calls on an excluded object class (console I/O), are not executed by the slice. They are admitted in a chain only if every observable bound field is identical before and after the live call."
 },
 "review": "Field correspondence is reviewed; offsets come from the kernel's BTF. f_mode keeps only bits the retained code consumes (READ, WRITE, LSEEK, PREAD, PWRITE, UNSIGNED_OFFSET, PATH, STREAM, BACKING). f_owner.signum is the signal number F_GETSIG reads and F_SETSIG writes. Object class 1 is a character device (console), class 2 a regular shmem file. Page-cache bytes use the arm64 VA_BITS=48/4K vmemmap-to-linear-map relation and require one non-internal xarray head entry. Each live file's dentry and inode bind to the dentry_pool and inode_pool entries at the file's class index, as in the model's initial layout; the file's f_path.dentry->d_inode must be its f_inode. i_mode keeps only the file-type bits (the retained code tests S_ISREG); append is i_flags & S_APPEND (1 << 2). Every inode's i_sb is the one model superblock, whose only field is the transient freeze-protection depth (sb_start_write/sb_end_write balance within a call). files.count.counter is the number of tasks sharing the descriptor table; __fget_light borrows the file without a reference when it is 1. The original read/write entries consume FMODE_ATOMIC_POS, CAN_READ, CAN_WRITE, WRITER and NONOTIFY too, and f_iocb_flags (IOCB_APPEND and friends); task.ioac holds the CONFIG_TASK_XACCT read/write counters they update. The file size is inode_pool[1].i_size (i_size of the class-2 inode). i_flags keeps S_NOATIME, S_IMMUTABLE, S_NOCMTIME, S_SWAPFILE, S_PRIVATE and S_NOSEC (S_APPEND stays the append member). The shmem_inode_info fields are read through container_of from the inode (seals, alloced, swapped, fallocend); the superblock flags and s_maxbytes, its bdi capabilities and the mount flags are configuration the model superblock and mount hold, checked as class-2 preconditions rather than bound, so state discovery does not treat mount options as per-call unknowns. task.flags keeps only PF_KTHREAD, the bit access_ok reads. The credential identifiers are kuid_t/kgid_t values (creds.uid.val and so on). The user namespace's uid_map and gid_map are bound from the live namespace (the initial one: user_ns.initial is level == 0); the model holds up to UID_GID_MAP_MAX_BASE_EXTENTS extents and the checkpoint check rejects more. Timestamps, i_version, i_state, folio flags and the coarse clock are model state the binding does not observe.",
 "preconditions": [
  {
   "path": ".signal->rlim[7].rlim_cur",
   "equals": 8,
   "reason": "the reviewed model returns rlimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE) as the constant 8 (f_dupfd and fd allocation bound new descriptors by it)"
  },
  {
   "path": ".signal->rlim[1].rlim_cur",
   "equals": 18446744073709551615,
   "reason": "the reviewed model returns rlimit(RLIMIT_FSIZE) as RLIM_INFINITY"
  }
 ]
